zed (e.g. always `pts` not `points`) across all tool responses |\n\n---\n\n### Distribution & Deployment\n\n**Backend**: Already on Render — keep it there. One env var: `DATABASE_URL`. The MCP server just needs the public URL.\n\n**MCP Server**: Python package using the `mcp` SDK (or `fastmcp` for simplicity).\n\nInstall on analyst's machine:\n```bash\npipx install nil-pro-mcp\n```\n\nConfigure in Claude Desktop (`~/Library/Application Support/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json`):\n```json\n{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"nil-pro\": {\n      \"command\": \"nil-pro-mcp\",\n      \"env\": {\n        \"NIL_PRO_API_URL\": \"https://your-render-app.onrender.com\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThat's the entire install for the analyst — one command, one config edit. No DB credentials, no Python knowledge needed. The API URL is the only secret.\n\n---\n\n### What the Analyst's Workflow Looks Like\n\n> \"Who are the best junior guards averaging at least 16 points in the Big 12?\"\n\nClaude calls `rank_players` → returns top 20 guards, sorted by rating, filtered to class=Junior, conference=Big 12, pts_min=16. Claude summarizes in plain English.\n\n> \"Tell me more about the top guy\"\n\nClaude calls `get_player_profile` with his `player_id`. Returns full breakdown including what's boosting/dragging his rating — which translates directly to \"here's what he needs to work on.\"\n\n> \"Who's he comparable to?\"\n\nClaude calls `find_comps`. Returns players with similar profiles — the analyst can use these as NIL market references.\n\n---\n\n### What to Build First\n\n1. Add `conference` to the materialized view (backend, ~30 min)\n2. Build the MCP server with all 6 tools (new `mcp/` directory in this repo)\n3. Test locally against the running backend\n4. Package for distribution\n\nWant me to start implementing? I'd suggest beginning with the backend conference change, then the MCP server.",
